@dengke li

Visually validated. * Most of the raw logs can be parsed with level=%{WORD:level} %{GREEDYDATA:content} time=%{TIMESTAMP_ISO8601:logdatetime}
* Only one multiline log ("QueryFailedError"). Right now, %{QUERYFAILEDERROR:specialcontext}:%{GREEDYDATA:content} is the grok pattern used, with the special token QUERYFAILEDERROR=>QueryFailerError. It will be good if the string "QueryFailedError" can be detected by Grok and a field called specialcontext will be assigned the string "QueryFailedError". If our ML algorithms can be told up front that specialcontext is non-empty the current log, it will be easier for the algorithm. Need to discuss with the team whether the field can be called specialcontext.
* One raw log is just a right curly brace ("}"). %{GREEDYDATA:content} is needed to deal with it.
